    "id": "sticky-notes",
    "name": "Sticky Notes",
    "description": "A workshop wall in a daylit studio: a bright whiteboard in an aluminium frame covered in square paper notes in soft colours, each with a short marker word, curled at the free edge over a soft shadow, plus dot stickers, marker-drawn lanes, headers and boxes, and a pad of notes on the ledge. Notes behave like real sticky notes as pure functions of time: they peel off the pad (the curl travels in from the free edge), fly, slap flat strip-first and flap down to a resting curl, then peel and hop between columns, cluster by colour, collect dot votes and ripple in a travelling breeze.",
